# GENERATED ARTIFACTS ARE LF, EVERYWHERE
#
# Git stores text as LF and, with core.autocrlf=true — the Windows
# default — writes CRLF into the working tree on checkout. That is fine
# for files a person edits. It is not fine for files a generator writes,
# because every `--check` compares what the generator produced (LF)
# against what is on disk (CRLF) and finds them different.
#
# The symptom is a gate that cannot pass. `gen-communication-reference.js
# --check` reported STALE on every Windows machine while CI, running on
# Linux, went green — so `npm run verify` was unusable on the only
# platform this repository is developed on, and the failure looked like a
# real staleness rather than a line-ending artefact.
#
# Two fixes exist and both are needed. Each checker normalises \r\n before
# comparing, which several already did. And the files are pinned to LF
# here, so the mismatch does not arise in the first place and the next
# generated artifact does not have to remember.
#
# Only generated output is pinned. Source files keep the platform default,
# because nothing compares those byte for byte.

# Registry-generated TypeScript
generated/*.ts        text eol=lf

# Generated reference documents
INFORMATION-ARCHITECTURE.html   text eol=lf
DESIGN-REFERENCE.html           text eol=lf
ASSEMBLY-REFERENCE.html         text eol=lf
PENDING-ASSEMBLIES.html         text eol=lf
GC-COMMUNICATION-SYSTEM.html    text eol=lf
WAVE-6-EXIT-GATE.html           text eol=lf

# Lifted from GC-ASSEMBLIES.html by gen-assembly-css.js
app/_assemblies/assemblies.css  text eol=lf

# Drizzle output. Applied verbatim against Postgres.
migrations/*.sql      text eol=lf
migrations/meta/*.json text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they do not run. The pre-commit gate is one.
*.sh                  text eol=lf
.githooks/*           text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.xlsx                binary
*.png                 binary
*.jpg                 binary
*.woff2               binary
